## Everything from Markdown still works

Plain **bold**, *italic*, ~~strike~~, `inline code`, [links](#callouts), autolinks like https://code.visualstudio.com, tables, lists and images.

| Feature        | `.md` | `.smd` |
| -------------- | :---: | :----: |
| Text & tables  |  ✅   |   ✅   |
| Colors         |  ❌   |   ✅   |
| Diagrams       |  ⚠️   |   ✅   |
| Validation     |  ❌   |   ✅   |

- [x] Every `.md` file is already a valid `.smd` file
- [x] Click a checkbox in the preview to toggle it in the source
- [ ] Try it now

## Inline styling

Use **named colors** that adapt to light and dark themes: [red]{color=red}, [orange]{color=orange}, [green]{color=green}, [blue]{color=blue}, [purple]{color=purple} — or any hex like [#0ea5e9]{color="#0ea5e9"}.

Combine attributes: [critical path]{color=red weight=bold}, [soft background]{bg=amber}, [outlined]{border=blue}, [big text]{size=lg}, [monospace]{font=mono}, [struck]{style=strike}. Highlight with ==double equals==.

Inline directives: :badge[Shipped]{color=green} :badge[Beta]{color=amber} :badge[Deprecated]{color=red} · :status[On track]{color=green} · :status[At risk]{color=red} · press :kbd[Ctrl+Shift+P] · ping :mention[@platform] · progress :progress{value=65}

## Callouts

:::note
A neutral note. Callouts can contain **any** Markdown, including lists and code.
:::

:::tip Pro tip
Custom titles go right after the name.
:::

:::warning{collapsible} Breaking change in v2 (click to expand)
The `render()` signature changed. Collapsible callouts start closed; use `{collapsible=open}` to start open.
:::

:::danger
Never commit secrets to the repository.
:::

:::success Deployed
Release 2.3.0 is live in all regions.
:::

:::question Open question
Should we support Windows ARM in the first release?
:::

