## For product & project managers

KPIs at a glance: :metric[42%]{label="Activation" delta="+3.1%" trend=up} :metric[1.8s]{label="p95 load" delta="-0.4s" trend=down good=down} :metric[312]{label="Open bugs" delta="+12" trend=up good=down}

- [ ] Finalize pricing page copy :priority[P1] @maya :due[2026-10-02]
- [ ] Legal review of new terms :priority[P0] @legal :due[2026-09-20]
- [x] Kickoff with design :priority[P2] @sam :due[2026-09-10]

:::decision{status=accepted date=2026-09-12 owner=@maya} Launch in the EU before the US
EU customers make up 60% of the waitlist, and the GDPR work is already done.
:::

:::decision{status=superseded date=2026-08-01 owner=@maya} Launch everywhere at once
Replaced by the EU-first decision above.
:::

:::risk{impact=high likelihood=medium owner=@ops status=open} Payment provider rate limits during launch
Pre-warm the connection pool and ask the provider for a temporary quota increase.
:::

:::timeline
- [x] **2026-09-01** — Discovery complete
- [x] **2026-09-15** — Design sign-off
- [ ] **2026-10-01** — Private beta
- [ ] **2026-11-01** — General availability
:::

## For developers

:::api{method=POST path="/v1/orders" auth="bearer token"} Create an order
| Field | Type | Required | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `items` | array | yes | At least one line item |
| `coupon` | string | no | Validated server-side |

**Responses:** `201` created · `409` duplicate idempotency key · `422` validation error
:::

Highlight lines with `{…}` after the language:

```ts title="src/retry.ts" {2,4-5}
export async function retry<T>(fn: () => Promise<T>, attempts = 3): Promise<T> {
  for (let i = 1; ; i++) {
    try { return await fn(); }
    catch (e) {
      if (i >= attempts) throw e;
    }
  }
}
```

Embed real source so docs never drift from the code (lines 1–12 of a file in this repo):

```ts file="src/pricing.ts" lines="1-12" {5}
```

## Background and history {agent=skip}

This section is marked `{agent=skip}`: it shows a "humans only" tag here, and `smd agent` leaves it out so agents don't pay for history they don't need.

## Audience-specific content

:::agent Implementation constraints
- Do not change the public API in `src/core/index.ts`.
- Run `npm test` and `smd validate` before proposing changes.
- Prefer named colors over hex values.
:::

:::human Why this matters
Agents get precise constraints; humans see a short rationale and can expand the agent notes when curious.
:::
